      "@type": "SemioticProjection",
      "instance_name": "semiotic_projection_1",
      "label": "User projected onto the visual representation of a 'dike' in the context of paying for pads",
      "description": "The user is projected onto the woman_in_foreground, who is visually depicted with a stern, unamused expression and crossed arms, embodying the stereotype described in the text. The text 'how dikes look when they're in line paying for their pads' explicitly maps this visual entity as the embodiment of the stereotype. The user sees themselves or identifies with the stereotype being projected onto this visual material. There are no explicit deictic pronouns like 'me' or 'you' in the text, but the meme's structure and the user's interpretation of the visual material as a self-referential stereotype create an implicit projection. The projection is onto the VisualMaterial entity 'woman_in_foreground' as the stereotypical 'dike' in the context of purchasing pads.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_8be65b56"
      },
